{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"not implemented|stub|mock|shim|placeholder|fake|TODO|todo|skip|setIntakeWalkHook|walkHook\" packages/lhc/src packages/lhc/test packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md'","aggregated_output":"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:19:- Idempotency: skip set from recorded keys, validation-before-skip precedence, `skipReason: duplicate_idempotency_key`, skips consume no order numbers, key-wins-over-content\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:20:- Event ordering: `MAX(event_order)` counter, dense sequence across batches and skips\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:47:- **AC-5.1**: Resending a fully recorded batch records nothing, skips every event, and reports each skip with its idempotency key.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:48:  - **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1): Record five, resend identically → zero recorded, five skips each carrying `skipReason: duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:49:- **AC-5.2**: Resending a batch where some events are recorded and some are new skips the recorded ones and records the new ones in batch order.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:50:  - **TC-5.2** (AC-5.2): Three old plus two new → three skips, two recorded continuing the order densely.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:53:- **AC-5.4** (event level): A skipped event causes no side effects.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:55:- **AC-5.5**: A valid event reusing a recorded key with different content is skipped; the original record is unchanged and the new content is not stored anywhere.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:56:  - **TC-5.5** (AC-5.5): Key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B → skipped, read-back returns A, B nowhere (`openRaw` scan).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:64:This story lands the epic's two highest-risk seams together, by design: the strict three-layer validation boundary and the batch transaction skeleton. The pipeline order is load-bearing: **validate → begin immediate → per event in array order [dedup-check → record] → result → commit.** Validation is pure and runs before the transaction, so a rejected batch never takes the write lock; validation precedes idempotency, so a duplicate key on a malformed event is a rejection, not a skip. The walk this story builds is the spine Stories 3–5 extend — projection, turn transitions, and work queueing each become one more step inside the same per-event iteration, which is why getting the skeleton right here is worth a heavy story.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:111:| TC-5.1 | `test/idempotency.test.ts` | full resend: five skips with `skipReason`, read-back unchanged |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:112:| TC-5.2 | `test/idempotency.test.ts` | partial resend: three skips, two recorded, dense order |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:114:| TC-5.4 | `test/idempotency.test.ts` | skips inert at event level (clause ladder continues S3–S5) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:115:| TC-5.5 | `test/idempotency.test.ts` | key K payload B resend → skipped, A intact, B nowhere (`openRaw` scan) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:131:- Batch result at this stage: `events[]` entries `{ idempotencyKey, outcome, skipReason? }` — no `messageId` until Story 3; `turnTransitions: []`, `queuedWork: []` until Stories 4–5; `threadPosition.lastEventOrder` live now.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:133:- The skip set is one `SELECT … WHERE idempotency_key IN (…)` at transaction start; the dedup decision reads only the key column (key-wins-over-content is the absence of a content comparison).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:139:- The mid-walk failure must be induced through a real mechanism (test seam closing the handle), and the assertion is post-reopen read-back — not a mocked transaction object reporting rollback.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:146:- Registration/default path: CLI router routes to the real surface, replacing Story 0 stubs; SDK exports the operation.\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/intake-seam.ts:6:  setIntakeWalkHook,\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts:96:export { setIntakeWalkHook, type IntakeWalkHook } from \"./intake-seam.js\";\npackages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts:42:      reason: `not implemented: ${op}`,\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process.test.ts:2:// verify-all only (needs a build artifact); plain verify announces the skip.\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process.test.ts:44:  it(\"a planned command reaches its fail-closed stub through the real binary\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process.test.ts:52:        reason: \"not implemented: messages.list\",\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:47:  it(\"TC-5.1: resending a fully recorded batch skips everything and changes nothing\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:62:      expect(entry.outcome).toBe(\"skipped\");\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:63:      expect(entry.skipReason).toBe(\"duplicate_idempotency_key\");\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:71:  it(\"TC-5.2: partial resend skips the old, records the new, and keeps the order dense\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:82:      \"skipped\",\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:83:      \"skipped\",\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:84:      \"skipped\",\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:113:  it(\"TC-5.4: skips are inert — no duplicate rows, no order numbers consumed, no transitions reported\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:122:    expect(resend.value.events.every((entry) => entry.outcome === \"skipped\")).toBe(true);\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:164:      outcome: \"skipped\",\npackages/lhc/test/idempotency.test.ts:165:      skipReason: \"duplicate_idempotency_key\",\npackages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:17:  setIntakeWalkHook,\npackages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:28:  setIntakeWalkHook(null);\npackages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:141:    setIntakeWalkHook((db, eventIndex) => {\npackages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:148:    setIntakeWalkHook(null);\npackages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:160:    setIntakeWalkHook((db, eventIndex) => {\npackages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:164:    setIntakeWalkHook(null);\npackages/lhc/test/smoke.test.ts:6:// still-stubbed commands remain on this list.\npackages/lhc/test/smoke.test.ts:54:  it(\"every planned command routes to a fail-closed stub with the exact stub error shape\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/smoke.test.ts:59:      expect(parsed, `stub shape for: ${argv.join(\" \")}`).toEqual({\npackages/lhc/test/smoke.test.ts:64:          reason: `not implemented: ${op}`,\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts:36:    outcome: \"recorded\" | \"skipped\";\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts:38:    skipReason?: \"duplicate_idempotency_key\";\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:17:// mocked transaction object.\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:19:let walkHook: IntakeWalkHook | null = null;\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:20:export function setIntakeWalkHook(hook: IntakeWalkHook | null): void {\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:21:  walkHook = hook;\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:39:// The skip set is read at transaction start and reads only the key column:\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:46:    const placeholders = chunk.map(() => \"?\").join(\", \");\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:48:      .prepare(`SELECT idempotency_key FROM event WHERE idempotency_key IN (${placeholders})`)\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:69:  // not a skip (validation-before-idempotency precedence).\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:94:    const skipSet = recordedKeys(\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:99:    // so skips consume no order numbers and the sequence stays dense.\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:109:      if (skipSet.has(event.idempotencyKey)) {\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:112:          outcome: \"skipped\",\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:113:          skipReason: \"duplicate_idempotency_key\",\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:126:        skipSet.add(event.idempotencyKey);\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:129:      walkHook?.(db, index);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
